<description>&lt;p&gt;The Nigerian army, using US intelligence support, killed eight terrorists and rescued 125 kidnapping victims while bandits killed two abducted people in Niger State despite a ransom, and President Tinubu reported four of eight top terrorist leaders killed or arrested. In Mali, the army rescued 24 personnel and received Mi-24 and Mi-8 helicopters and an Il-76 transport, while 300 Russian mercenaries were killed. A Protestant missionary abducted in Niger was released and thousands of Arab nomads were ordered to leave southeast Niger. Al-Qaeda and ISIS fighting is escalating in the Sahel and Burkina Faso is targeting critics in exile. The conflict caused 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Demócrata&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE5oaldvZGc3R01yM0d3ZUVEczdzRmVCWnA0OE1FaFBITGp3dXYwd1RtaERhWmFNblhLbmtQczBBaXB0UjFncUlpcndiUlJOY0VReTVVZXR4QXBwOTJBMEwwR19fejItSXJzeE9JZWpLaUNhSU9PbVRCT01uU3pQUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Human Rights Watch&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiaEFVX3lxTE9lcjJkSkFFaFlIWXZlU1FCMW9Mb2lwQjl1M01OVEtWdThDbGhKUUNwNHZlbHRHRTVfS0gyX2doZ0pEWGdRMXhCaG5YOVplRFFRaUF2MnVUSXpxci1nWlVJVFZrbnRKZ0oy?oc=5&quot;&gt;Envanter Medya&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPTzJ5eVR4NWJ5ZDlqVU4zZ3FjaUtvSHRpU3VuN3JKaC1kczltc2VPT2M3UVBnQnpaRmh3aWdKTkhuUWNWWG9uV1lvMGxicEw0bXZLVmxoMElSV0pJR0M3R0hFSFFCcW5EY1JPNG1nMF9RN2VtUzBhQUkzQ2wtX0o3YVdpLWVMSXpjSFRrRmJxbW5QZWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Il Sole 24 ORE&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiygFBVV95cUxQSVJnbnZfMVk0UkdUWHlNdTdSREVqYWZIenBnQlRtU2hNSjljYkd5ckFrNl93RFJNM3FhRHk1VDVOTFdHY2VTTVNNUHBCTndOUjJlYm9jOExzU0Z4Q1FnYXZYT2ZtRmU1azJZZ0hjeWlQUGRiUVpPRDU4dUI1UHpLckdtVmtP